course: dictionary
lesson: 2301
title: The word crisis
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A crisis is a time of great danger, difficulty or trouble, when important decisions must be made. «Staying calm in a crisis lets you do something useful, such as fetching a teacher.» Here a crisis is an emergency, and fetching a teacher is how you get help.
explain: Crisis can also mean a turning point, a moment when things will get either much better or much worse. Historians use the phrase «Suez Crisis» for the trouble after Egypt took over the Suez Canal in 1956. Words like energy, food and health often come before crisis to name the problem, as in «the cost of living crisis».
explain: Words around crisis show you which meaning is used. In a news report or a story, the danger is real. «Hair crisis» is a joke about a small problem. Ask yourself: is anyone really in danger or trouble? If not, the word is probably being used jokingly.
fact: A crisis is a time of great danger, difficulty or trouble.
fact: The plural of crisis is crises.
fact: «Crisis» can mean a turning point, when things will get either much better or much worse.
fact: People sometimes joke that a small problem is a crisis, like a hair crisis.
fact: In March 2021 the giant ship «Ever Given» got stuck across the Suez Canal for six days, holding up hundreds of ships.
exercise: «Staying calm in a crisis lets you do something useful, such as fetching a teacher.» What is a crisis here? | A kind of food | A type of teacher | A fun game played at break | *A time of great danger or trouble, when you need help
exercise: Ella says her «hair crisis» is serious. What does the joking use of crisis mean? | A famous old castle | A school rule | A real disaster in the city | *A small problem that people make a fuss about
exercise: Which word is the plural of crisis? | crisis's | crisises | *crises | crisi
test: Which sentence uses crisis for a serious emergency? | *«Families used food banks during the cost of living crisis.» | «The crisis was a fun joke at break.» | «Our class had a hair crisis before the photo.» | «My crisis is my new shoes.»
test: What must happen in a crisis? | Everyone must go home | Nothing, you just wait | *Important decisions must be made | Books must be read aloud
exam: How can you tell whether «crisis» in a text is serious or a joke? | Skip the whole text | *Read the words around it and ask whether anyone is really in danger | Guess at random and move on | Count the letters in the word
